message: "If you use this artifact or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Token-Accounting Integrity in LLM Metering: A Systematic Study of Client-Side Under-Payment"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible testbed, attack harness, defense implementations, TLA+ model and
  measurement corpus for client-side under-payment in LLM metering architectures under an
  honest-provider threat model. The work decomposes the failure space into state
  synchronization (B0), commitment timing (M1) and usage authority (M2), unified by the
  accounting-integrity property V(r) <= N(r), and pairs every attack with a defense.
